A host keeps one factory for each extension file, whichever folder loads it.

pi caches the factories it loads for one folder and empties the cache
whenever a load comes from another, with jiti's module cache off. A host
opens and wakes conversations in many folders, so each open or wake in a
folder other than the last evaluated every extension's modules again: the
host's loop stalled for seconds each time and its memory grew with every
copy. The folder reaches an extension only through the API its factory is
given, so one cache now serves every folder, keyed by the file the
extension's path resolves to: folders loading the same file share its
factory, and a folder's own extension, another file, stays its own. Each
extension made from a factory holds it and the cache holds it weakly, so
it stays while any live conversation holds its extensions, and the copy a
moved link pointed at goes once its last conversation ends rather than
living until a reload. A reload still empties the cache, and a load begun
before one caches nothing after it.

